INSERT INTO `core_jarvisknowledge` VALUES
(14,'Honda Click 125i won\'t accelerate properly','honda click 125i won accelerate properly','125i accelerate click honda properly won','test answer',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 11:07:25.107800','2026-11-16 11:07:25.107812','','2026-12-16 11:07:25.091416','general','english','','','','2026-11-16 11:07:25.091416',''),
(15,'where  i can find battery terminals','find battery terminal','battery find terminal','On your 2022 Suzuki Raider, Glenn, the battery is located under the seat. You will need to remove the seat by accessing the release mechanism, which is typically found near the rear of the side panels or under the tail section depending on the specific sub-model configuration.\n\nOnce the seat is removed, you will see a plastic cover or a rubber strap securing the battery; the positive (red) and negative (black) terminals will be clearly visible on top of the battery unit.\n\n**Safety Note:** Always ensure the ignition is switched to OFF before touching the terminals to prevent accidental shorting with your wrench.\n\n[chips: How to test battery voltage | How to check the main fuse | What if the battery is fine?]',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 15:52:15.049785','2026-11-16 15:52:15.049810','','2026-12-16 15:52:15.034988','general','english','','','','2026-11-16 15:52:15.034988',''),
(16,'provide an image','provide image','image provide','Certainly, sir. I have access to our technical library for all motorcycle components. Which specific part are you interested in inspecting today? \n\nPlease specify the part name (e.g., Brake Caliper, Spark Plug, CVT, Radiator, etc.), and I will provide the visual diagram and inspection criteria immediately. \n\n[chips: Brake Caliper | Spark Plug | CVT Variator | Radiator | Battery]',2,'gemini','2026-11-16 15:58:42.192646','2026-11-16 16:01:17.398687','','2026-12-16 16:01:17.390628','general','english','','','','2026-11-16 16:01:17.390628',''),
(17,'where is it located','located','located','It appears we have lost the thread of our previous discussion, sir. Since I am unable to reference a specific part from our current history, could you clarify which component you are inquiring about?\n\nTypically, motorcycle components are housed in consistent areas, but their exact placement varies by design. Once you specify the part, I can provide its general location and the necessary safety precautions for accessing it.\n\n[chips: Where is the battery? | Where is the spark plug? | Where is the air filter? | Where is the oil filter? | Where is the fuse box?]',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 15:58:49.989018','2026-11-16 15:58:49.989032','','2026-12-16 15:58:49.987042','general','english','','','','2026-11-16 15:58:49.987042',''),
(18,'can you show me where to look','you show look','look show you','I suspect you are referring to the location of a specific maintenance component, sir. Since the location of parts varies significantly by design, I have provided the typical locations for the most common items below:\n\n*   **Oil Filter:** Usually found on the side or bottom of the engine crankcase, hidden behind a small circular cover or as an external spin-on canister.\n*   **Air Filter:** Typically housed inside the airbox, which is generally located under the seat or behind a side panel.\n*   **Battery:** Most commonly located under the seat, behind a side panel, or occasionally under the front fairing on certain scooter models.\n*   **Spark Plug:** Found at the top or center of the cylinder head, sometimes requiring you to lift the fuel tank or remove a small access cover.\n*   **Fuse Box:** Usually situated near the battery, under the seat, or behind a side cover.\n\nPlease confirm in your owner\'s manual for the exact layout of your machine, as manufacturers enjoy rearranging these components for the sake of ergonomics and packaging. If you had a different component in mind, do let me know so I can point you in the right direction.\n\n[chips: Where is the battery? | Locate the spark plug | How to find the air filter | Checking oil levels]',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 15:58:58.544677','2026-11-16 15:58:58.544687','','2026-12-16 15:58:58.542922','general','english','','','','2026-11-16 15:58:58.542922',''),
(19,'Help & capabilities','capabilitie','capabilitie','Hello. I am J.A.R.V.I.S. I have been initialized and synchronized with your Yamaha Sniper 150. As your diagnostic tutor, I am prepared to assist you in maintaining or repairing your machine with precision. \n\nSince you requested information on my capabilities, I am equipped to guide you through:\n*   **Engine Performance:** Troubleshooting EFI systems, ignition timing, and fuel delivery.\n*   **Drivetrain & Transmission:** Clutch adjustments and chain maintenance.\n*   **Electrical Systems:** Stator, rectifier, battery, and lighting circuits.\n*   **Chassis & Braking:** Brake system maintenance and suspension adjustments.\n\nBecause you have not yet reported a specific fault, I am currently in \"Standby/Monitoring\" mode. To begin a diagnostic session, please provide a specific symptom (e.g., \"The engine cranks but won\'t start,\" \"The brake lever feels spongy,\" or \"The FI light is flashing a code\").\n\nOnce you provide a symptom, I will generate a formal diagnostic protocol following the 9-part structure required for your safety and success.\n\n**How can I assist you with your Sniper 150 today?**\n\n[chips: Start Engine Diagnostics | Start Electrical Diagnostics | Brake/Chassis Help | View Maintenance Schedule]',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 16:16:36.735668','2026-11-16 16:16:36.735683','','2026-12-16 16:16:36.731818','diagnostic','english','Yamaha','Sniper 150','','2026-11-16 16:16:36.731818',''),
(20,'My motorcycle won\'t start. The starter clicks or makes no sound.','motorcycle won start starter click make sound','click make motorcycle sound start starter won','To safely diagnose your starting issue, please ensure the scooter is in neutral and on its center stand. What is the engine displacement of your scooter, and is it fuel-injected (FI) or carbureted (carb)?',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 17:05:39.700214','2026-11-16 17:05:39.700233','','2026-12-16 17:05:39.695120','diagnose starting issue','english','','','','2026-11-16 17:05:39.695120',''),
(21,'My motorcycle battery keeps draining or is not charging while running.','motorcycle battery keep draining not charging while running','battery charging draining keep motorcycle not running while','A draining battery often points to a failure in the charging system, such as the stator or rectifier-regulator. To narrow this down, what is the engine displacement of your motorcycle, and is it fuel-injected (FI) or carbureted (Carb)?',1,'gemini','2026-11-16 17:26:12.566557','2026-11-16 17:26:12.566570','','2026-12-16 17:26:12.463513','diagnose_charging_system','english','','','','2026-11-16 17:26:12.463513','');
